# SAD routing

This project follows the **Stakeholder-Anchored Development** methodology. The single source of truth for project policy is `.sad/memory/constitution.md`. The single operational entry point is `AGENTS.md` at the repo root.

## Rule precedence (do not violate)

1. `.sad/memory/constitution.md` (immutable project policy)
2. `AGENTS.md` (operational entry point)
3. `.cursor/rules/` (this file and any siblings — tool-mechanical only)
4. user-level rules
5. assistant defaults

If you detect a conflict, surface it. Do not silently follow a lower-layer rule that contradicts the constitution.

## Quick orientation

- Lifecycle: `LIFECYCLE.md` (14 numbered steps; full diagram in `CHEATSHEET.md`).
- Always-loaded short rules: `.sad/rules/core/README.md` (SAD-CR-001 .. 004).
- Three-tier audience model: every feature produces three walkthroughs (`walkthroughs/{non-technical,semi-technical,technical}.md`); approval gate requires all three.
- Maturity level for this project: see `.sad/memory/constitution.md` Identity section.

## When a /sad-* command is invoked

Read the canonical prompt at `commands/sad-<command>.md`. Follow its `Your task` and `Discipline` sections exactly. Do not improvise tier-routing or approval semantics.
